bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    capture_write_check_misses_mutating_method_calls_2026_11_10, 0, "2026-11-10 census (heuristic awk over multi-line and inline backslash lambdas, module globals excluded): src/ 0 sites; test/ 15 local sites (iter_deprecated_spec x2 trees, chars_deprecated_spec x2, deprecated_removed_spec in test/03_system, and the policy pin closure_capture_writeback_spec:76 which asserts the dropped push). Nested-fn sites could not be censused by grep and receiver type (class reference vs value array) is unknown at parse level, so the check is staged as warning W-CAPTURE-MUTATION, not an error. Fix: seed find_captured_local_mutations + CaptureMutation (parser/src/capture_write_check.rs), eprinted by module_loader reject_captured_local_writes and native_project compiler; pure-Simple twin capture_write_warnings() eprinted by interpreter/mod.spl and _FlatAstBridge/module_assembly.spl. User me-method calls not covered (no type info). Specs: test/01_unit/compiler/frontend/capture_mutation_warning_spec.spl red 1/3 -> green 3/3; seed cargo tests capture_write_check (4 new); closure_capture_writeback_spec 7/7 and deprecated_removed_spec 13/13 stay green. Follow-up: promote to error after migrating the 15 test sites."
